<title>CANADA: Novopharm ordered to pay C$5.4 mln to Apotex.</title>
<headline>Novopharm ordered to pay C$5.4 mln to Apotex.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manitoba Court found on Thursday that privately held Novopharm Ltd misappropriated technology from privately held Apotex Inc, and ordered Novopharm to pay C$5.4 million in damages and interest plus court costs.</p>
<p>The court also told Novopharm from doing any further work on a group of generic anticholesterol drugs until January 1, 1998.</p>
<p>The case, which began in August 1993, found that a Novopharm employee stole scientific data and product samples from Apotex.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
</text>
